    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1">

                <pb facs="0291" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg167"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Argentine Minister of Foreign Affairs and
                        Worship</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fueyrredon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to address Your
                    Excellency for the purpose of informing you that the Government of Costa Rica
                    has sent to this Department a note, a certified copy of which is enclosed<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d147-f1"/> to the effect that it does not suit that
                    Government to continue being a party to the Trade Mark Convention signed at the
                    Fourth International American Conference which met in this capital in 1910,
                    wherefor it sees fit to denounce it.</p>
                <pb facs="0292" n="168" xml:id="pg168"/>
                <p>Consequently and in accordance with the provision in Article XIX of the
                    above-named Convention I forward that instrument to Your Excellency by way of
                    notification and for the information of Your Government.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Pueyrredon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="61" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Costa Rican communication was dated Sept. 30, 1921.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
